# Consolidation of SLH-D-0004

Written by Alice, the observer, at 2026-11-23 02:55. This document closes the
discussion.

## The golden token

The token of this discussion is mango. Bob, Carol, Dave and Percy each
returned it, in the last entry of their file and in their message to the
observer.

## What each agent found

| Agent | Angle | Findings | The most serious |
|---|---|---|---|
| [Dave](dave.hmd) | the data | 6 | Every cell matched its header. Two closing times were the times the files were created, earlier than the commits their outcomes name |
| [Percy](percy.hmd) | the reader | 10 | The card said the list in the rules follows by itself, and the rules said it is kept by hand |
| [Bob](bob.hmd) | the code | 11 | Twenty-four malformed headers tried, and all of them silent: a brief with a field missing removed its discussion from the report |
| [Carol](carol.hmd) | the design | 8 | "Closed" was matched by a declared field and not by the folder, so one wrong digit showed a closed discussion open |

Three of the four came to the same fault from different sides: the report
was right on the day and said nothing when a header was wrong.

## What was changed

- **The rows are built from the folders,** and the headers are joined to
  them, as Carol proposed. A header that does not fit leaves a question
  mark in its row and cannot remove the row.
- **A table of problems,** as Bob and Carol proposed: a header that does
  not fit, a name that differs between a header and its folder, a time
  that is not a time, a token used twice, a closed discussion whose token
  a worker did not return.
- **A brief is a brief by its category,** and a consolidation is the file
  of that name in the folder.
- **Agents are named by their files,** and only files directly in the
  folder count.
- **`returned` in the header of a consolidation,** as Carol proposed, so
  that the rule of the token is something the report checks.
- **The order is by number,** and no longer by a time someone typed.
- **Cells are escaped,** so a bar in a topic cannot break a row.
- **One list of discussions.** The list kept by hand in the rules is gone.
- **The card:** examples that cannot be mistaken for a real discussion,
  the steps for opening and closing in one place, what "conclusive" means
  above the table, and what the render command does to the file.
- **The two closing times** Dave found are corrected to the times of the
  commits.

I tried the new module on a copy with four headers broken on purpose. Each
row stayed, and each fault was listed.

## Not changed

- **A check that fails.** The render succeeds whatever it lists. Bob asks
  for a way a script can fail on it. Not built.
- **The roster as data.** Carol proposes holding the roster in a header, so
  that a file that is not an agent's can be told from one that is. Not
  built: every file in a folder still counts as an agent.
- **Times that are not from a clock.** Dave and Percy note that times in
  the workers' files, and the opening times of the first discussions,
  cannot be confirmed.
